From f76be9a99d1bcdc62ec9d14972256fc848251487 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:16:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] k1om-*-linux: runtime libraries

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6: libgcc, libstdc++, libgomp, libitm, libffi,
libgfortran, libsanitizer, libgo and libtool treat k1om-*-linux* like
x86_64-*-linux*.  libgcc additionally builds the soft-fp TF routines
and crtprec*/crtfastmath and uses the x86 Linux unwinder; decimal float
is BID.  libgcc builds none of the _Float16/__bf16 routines (upstream
compiles them with -msse2): the compiler still provides both types for
the intrinsic headers, but libgcc is built without HF/BF support.
libsanitizer does not emit prefetchnta (no SSE) and does without
<scsi/scsi.h>.

Configure scripts are regenerated from their sources.  Intel's tree had
them sed-edited instead, partly without the matching source change: the
x86 -fpic choice in config/picflag.m4 is carried here as a source
change; k1om in autoconf's own AC_C_BIGENDIAN darwin -arch list, in
libitm's AVX/RTM and libstdc++'s rdrand assembler probes (which fail
for k1om regardless) and a hard-wired libgcc_cv_lib_sjlj_exceptions=no
are dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
